{"timestamp":"07:05:45.373","source":"Browser","level":"LOG","message":"[extractPracticeNames] currentDoc: {\"activities\":[],\"activitySpaces\":[],\"alphas\":[],\"baselinePracticeName\":\"Platform Adoption Essentials\",\"description\":\"This coordinating macro-practice orchestrates the entire Ansible Automation Platform 2.6 adoption lifecycle. It explicitly does not define new Alphas, Activities, or discrete Work Products. Instead, it establishes an overarching temporal framework—via comprehensive Patterns—that accurately tracks the simultaneous progression of architectural planning, containerized physical deployment, access governance, and mesh scaling across unified organizational delivery phases.\",\"name\":\"AAP 2.6 Lifecycle Orchestration Practice\",\"narratives\":[{\"description\":\"How the four disparate practices compose into a single unified lifecycle\",\"name\":\"Orchestration Overview\",\"narrativeContexts\":[{\"context\":\"Enterprise platform engineering simply cannot occur in isolated silos. High-level architecture must seamlessly inform infrastructure provisioning, which must be physically verified before complex governance policies and distributed mesh networks can be applied safely.\",\"narrativeElementName\":\"Prerequisites\",\"seq\":1},{\"context\":\"This Lifecycle pattern coordinates these distinct capability domains, ensuring that organizations achieve operational maturity sequentially and logically. For example, the Deployment Topology must reach the Baselined state before the Installation Configuration is permitted to enter the Executed state, explicitly preventing costly deployment rework. By observing the Pattern View Matrix, technology leaders can track the holistic health of the automation rollout, ensuring that security (RBAC) and scale (Mesh) mature in lockstep with the core infrastructure platform.\",\"narrativeElementName\":\"Lifecycle Phase\",\"seq\":2}],\"narrativeName\":\"The Complete Platform Adoption Journey\",\"narrativeTypeName\":\"Lifecycle\"}],\"patterns\":[{\"description\":\"The end-to-end orchestration of planning, installing, securing, and scaling the platform ecosystem.\",\"name\":\"AAP 2.6 Enterprise Adoption Lifecycle\",\"narrativeTypeName\":\"Lifecycle\",\"narratives\":[{\"description\":\"The sequential approach to deploying AAP 2.6 effectively.\",\"name\":\"Adoption Lifecycle Context\",\"narrativeContexts\":\"[Array]\",\"narrativeName\":\"Orchestrating the Entire Rollout\",\"narrativeTypeName\":\"Lifecycle\"}],\"patternViews\":[{\"alphaStates\":\"[Array]\",\"description\":\"Securing enterprise subscriptions, evaluating basic workloads, and establishing a baseline understanding of capability needs.\",\"name\":\"Prerequisites Phase\",\"seq\":0},{\"alphaStates\":\"[Array]\",\"description\":\"Finalizing exhaustive system blueprints, provisioning the base RHEL host nodes, and finalizing the exact configurations to be injected.\",\"name\":\"Architecture and Preparation Phase\",\"seq\":1},{\"alphaStates\":\"[Array]\",\"description\":\"Executing the configuration-as-code installer playbooks and rigorously validating that core rootless container services are active.\",\"name\":\"Container Deployment Phase\",\"seq\":2},{\"alphaStates\":\"[Array]\",\"description\":\"Hardening access controls via the Gateway, integrating SSO, and deploying the initial layers of the automation mesh.\",\"name\":\"Governance and Day-2 Operations Phase\",\"seq\":3},{\"alphaStates\":\"[Array]\",\"description\":\"Reaching peak maturity by fully automating governance and verifying edge execution resilience.\",\"name\":\"Enterprise Scale Phase\",\"seq\":4}]}],\"personaGroups\":[],\"personas\":[],\"workProducts\":[]}"}
