yName\":\"Management\",\"description\":\"Extends to new contexts\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Innovating\"}],\"name\":\"Management\"},{\"description\":\"The ability to design, implement, and automate security policies, access controls, and compliance checks within the platform.\",\"levels\":[{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Security And Compliance Enforcement\",\"description\":\"Understands basic security principles and compliance requirements.\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Basic\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Security And Compliance Enforcement\",\"description\":\"Can configure basic security settings and access controls based on documented procedures.\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Applies\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Security And Compliance Enforcement\",\"description\":\"Can independently design and implement comprehensive security architectures and automate compliance auditing.\",\"level\":3,\"name\":\"Masters\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Security And Compliance Enforcement\",\"description\":\"Can adapt security strategies to address novel threats and complex, multi-cloud environments.\",\"level\":4,\"name\":\"Adapts\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Security And Compliance Enforcement\",\"description\":\"Develops new paradigms for platform security and proactive threat hunting.\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Innovating\"}],\"name\":\"Platform Security And Compliance Enforcement\"},{\"description\":\"The ability to align platform capabilities and roadmap with broader business goals, economic models, and enterprise architecture.\",\"levels\":[{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Strategic Alignment\",\"description\":\"Understands the high-level business drivers for the platform.\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Basic\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Strategic Alignment\",\"description\":\"Can articulate how specific platform features support identified business opportunities.\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Applies\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Strategic Alignment\",\"description\":\"Can develop and manage platform roadmaps that demonstrably drive business value and ROI.\",\"level\":3,\"name\":\"Masters\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Strategic Alignment\",\"description\":\"Can pivot platform strategy in response to shifting market conditions or major organizational changes.\",\"level\":4,\"name\":\"Adapts\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Platform Strategic Alignment\",\"description\":\"Pioneers new platform business models or economic strategies that redefine enterprise value.\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Innovating\"}],\"name\":\"Platform Strategic Alignment\"},{\"description\":\"The ability to apply software engineering principles to operations, ensuring platform reliability, scalability, and performance (SRE).\",\"levels\":[{\"competencyName\":\"Site Reliability\",\"description\":\"Understands the concepts of SLIs, SLOs, and basic incident response.\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Basic\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Site Reliability\",\"description\":\"Can participate in incident response and implement basic monitoring alerts.\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Applies\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Site Reliability\",\"description\":\"Can independently design robust monitoring systems, define effective SLOs, and lead complex incident resolutions.\",\"level\":3,\"name\":\"Masters\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Site Reliability\",\"description\":\"Can architect highly resilient, self-healing systems and establish enterprise-wide SRE practices.\",\"level\":4,\"name\":\"Adapts\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Site Reliability\",\"description\":\"Develops novel approaches to chaos engineering or predictive reliability modeling.\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Innovating\"}],\"name\":\"Site Reliability\"},{\"description\":\"The ability to gather, communicate, and balance the needs of other stakeholders, and accurately represent their views.\",\"levels\":[{\"competencyName\":\"Stakeholder Representation\",\"description\":\"Fundamental awareness and understanding of representation concepts.\",\"level\":1,\"name\":\"Basic\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Stakeholder Representation\",\"description\":\"Can apply representation concepts in simple contexts.\",\"level\":2,\"name\":\"Applies\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Stakeholder Representation\",\"description\":\"Can apply representation concepts in most contexts without supervision.\",\"level\":3,\"name\":\"Masters\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Stakeholder Representation\",\"description\":\"Can apply judgment and adapt representation techniques to complex contexts.\",\"level\":4,\"name\":\"Adapts\"},{\"competencyName\":\"Stakeholder Representation\",\"description\":\"Recognized expert, able to extend representation concepts to new contexts.\",\"level\":5,\"name\":\"Innovating\"}],\"name\":\"Stakeholder Representation\"}],\"createdAt\":\"2023-10-25T00:00:00Z\",\"description\":\"The Platform Adoption Kernel establishes the universal foundation for platform transformations, organized into the three Areas of Concern.\",\"focuses\":[{\"description\":\"Focuses on business justification, financial management, and organizational alignment.\",\"name\":\"Value\"},{\"description\":\"Encapsulates the design, provisioning, optimization, and the hosted items running on the platform foundation.\",\"name\":\"Solution\"},{\"description\":\"Governs the execution of the transformation, encompassing people, processes, and policies.\",\"name\":\"Endeavor\"}],\"keywords\":[\"platform\",\"adoption\",\"kernel\"],\"name\":\"Platform Adoption Essentials\",\"narrativeTypes\":[{\"description\":\"Enforces a strict cause-and-effect relationship between context and outcomes (Situation, Task, Action, Result).\",\"name\":\"The STAR Format\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"The context or background of the challenge.\",\"howToUse\":\"Describe the specific situation, context, or baseline state before action is taken.\",\"name\":\"Situation\"},{\"description\":\"The specific challenge, objective, or requirement.\",\"howToUse\":\"Outline the specific task, problem, or goal that needs to be addressed.\",\"name\":\"Task\"},{\"description\":\"The specific steps or interventions performed.\",\"howToUse\":\"Detail the methodology, activities, or steps taken to address the task.\",\"name\":\"Action\"},{\"description\":\"The outcome, impact, or value achieved.\",\"howToUse\":\"Summarize the measurable results, outcomes, or state changes achieved from the actions.\",\"name\":\"Result\"}]},{\"description\":\"Highly effective for macro-level lifecycle orchestrations (platform adoptions, transformations).\",\"name\":\"The Hero's Journey\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"The starting point before the transformation.\",\"howToUse\":\"Describe the current, pre-platform state of the organization.\",\"name\":\"The Ordinary World\"},{\"description\":\"The catalyst for change.\",\"howToUse\":\"Outline the business opportunity, crisis, or driver that necessitates the platform transformation.\",\"name\":\"The Call to Adventure\"},{\"description\":\"The core transformation challenges and execution.\",\"howToUse\":\"Detail the complex adoption activities, migrations, and challenges faced during implementation.\",\"name\":\"The Ordeal\"},{\"description\":\"The new operational baseline and realized value.\",\"howToUse\":\"Describe the successful adoption, the accrual of benefits, and the new optimized way of working.\",\"name\":\"The Return\"}]},{\"description\":\"Positions the consumer as the Hero and the Platform Engineering team as the Guide utilizing the defined approach.\",\"name\":\"The Three-Act Structure & StoryBrand\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"Identifying the consumer and their pain points.\",\"howToUse\":\"Identify the primary consumer (the Hero) and detail the specific friction or problem they face.\",\"name\":\"Act I: The Hero and the Problem\"},{\"description\":\"The platform team offers a solution.\",\"howToUse\":\"Introduce the Platform Engineering team as the Guide who provides a clear, paved-path approach or plan.\",\"name\":\"Act II: The Guide and the Plan\"},{\"description\":\"Execution and outcome.\",\"howToUse\":\"Describe the call to action for the consumer to adopt the plan, and the successful outcome of doing so.\",\"name\":\"Act III: Call to Action and Success\"}]},{\"description\":\"Shorter frameworks (And/But/Therefore) designed for rapid, highly persuasive daily execution updates.\",\"name\":\"Micro-Narratives (ABT)\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"The current situation and baseline facts.\",\"howToUse\":\"State the current agreed-upon context, background, and baseline facts.\",\"name\":\"And (Context)\"},{\"description\":\"The problem, challenge, or contradiction.\",\"howToUse\":\"Introduce the specific problem, blocker, challenge, or contradiction encountered.\",\"name\":\"But (Conflict)\"},{\"description\":\"The action taken or conclusion reached.\",\"howToUse\":\"State the specific action taken, decision made, or conclusion reached to resolve the conflict.\",\"name\":\"Therefore (Resolution)\"}]},{\"description\":\"A brief, informal explanation of a software feature written from the perspective of the end user.\",\"name\":\"User story\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"This identifies the specific persona or role interacting with the feature. It avoids the generic term **the user** to provide context on their technical ability, permissions, and needs.\",\"howToUse\":\"Use this to define constraints. Instead of saying \\\"user,\\\" say \\\"First-time Visitor\\\" or \\\"System Administrator.\\\" This helps the developers understand if the UI should be \\\"idiot-proof\\\" or \\\"power-user focused.\\\"\",\"name\":\"As a [role]\"},{\"description\":\"This is the intent or the feature itself. It describes the action the user wants to take within the software.\",\"howToUse\":\"Keep this focused on the **what,** not the **how.** Avoid mentioning specific UI elements like **click a red button.** Focus on the functional capability you are giving them.\",\"name\":\"I wan to [perform some action]\"},{\"description\":\"This is the purpose. It explains the underlying problem the user is trying to solve or the value they hope to gain.\",\"howToUse\":\"Use this to justify the work. If you can’t find a compelling **So that** statement, the feature might not be worth building. It also helps developers suggest better technical solutions if they understand the ultimate goal.\",\"name\":\"So that [I can achieve some goal]\"}]},{\"description\":\"A well-structured Epic provides a \\\"north star\\\" for the team, ensuring everyone knows why a large project exists and what success looks like.\",\"name\":\"Epic\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"A clear, punchy title and a one-sentence elevator pitch that describes the high-level initiative.\",\"howToUse\":\"Treat this as the project's identity. Use it in stakeholder meetings and roadmap views to provide an instant understanding of what is being built without getting bogged down in details.\",\"name\":\"Summary\"},{\"description\":\"This section explains how this Epic aligns with the company's broader business goals or quarterly objectives (OKRs).\",\"howToUse\":\"Use this to justify the budget and resource allocation. If you can't link the Epic back to a specific business value (e.g., \\\"Increasing retention by 10%\\\"), it shouldn't be an Epic.\",\"name\":\"Strategic Intent\"},{\"description\":\"A list of the primary and secondary users who will be impacted by this large-scale change.\",\"howToUse\":\"Use this to keep the scope focused. When brainstorming features, ask: \\\"Does this specific feature serve the personas listed in the Epic?\\\" If not, it belongs in a different Epic.\",\"name\":\"User Personas\"},{\"description\":\"These are not detailed stories yet, but rather the broad capabilities the system must have once the Epic is finished.\",\"howToUse\":\"Use these as \\\"themes\\\" to help you brainstorm the individual User Stories later. They serve as the framework for your backlog.\",\"name\":\"High-Level Requirements\"},{\"description\":\"The quantitative data points that will prove the Epic was a success after it is released.\",\"howToUse\":\"Use this to define the \\\"Definition of Done\\\" for the entire project. Instead of saying \\\"when the code is finished,\\\" use \\\"when the checkout conversion rate hits 5%.\\\"\",\"name\":\"Success Metrics\"}]},{\"description\":\"A standard lifecycle orchestration framework to map progression phases.\",\"name\":\"Lifecycle\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"Conditions required before starting the lifecycle.\",\"howToUse\":\"Define the Phase 0 or preparation steps, including baseline checks or prerequisite states, that must be achieved before the main lifecycle begins.\",\"name\":\"Prerequisites\"},{\"description\":\"An active stage of lifecycle execution.\",\"howToUse\":\"Detail the active state transitions, required work products, and activities for this specific phase of the lifecycle progression.\",\"name\":\"Lifecycle Phase\"}]},{\"description\":\"A cohesive narrative format that guides the reader carefully through the evidence for and against a proposition before reaching a conclusion.\",\"name\":\"Essay Narrative\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"The start of the essay used to contextualise the work and grab the attention of the reader.\",\"howToUse\":\"Explain how the topic sits within the framework of the subject area as a whole. Outline the structure of your essay very briefly, but do not give your conclusions away on the first page.\",\"name\":\"Introduction\"},{\"description\":\"A section establishing the interpretation of central concepts without relying on dictionary definitions.\",\"howToUse\":\"Relate in your own words how the terms you will be using are to be interpreted within the context of your essay.\",\"name\":\"Defining Key Concepts\"},{\"description\":\"The core discussion where secondary works are evaluated and viewpoints are balanced against each other.\",\"howToUse\":\"Be selective in your choice of evidence and use signposting language to guide your reader. Quote sparingly, paraphrase occasionally, and summarise often to integrate other people's ideas into your own argument.\",\"name\":\"Presenting Evidence\"},{\"description\":\"The closing section that synthesises the presented evidence and forms a direct response to the assignment title.\",\"howToUse\":\"Draw the threads of your argument together. Do not bring in new evidence in your concluding paragraphs or try to cram in ideas that you have not developed fully.\",\"name\":\"Conclusion\"}]},{\"description\":\"A formal, informative structure broken down into sections and sub-sections to order and communicate relevant information in an easily navigable way.\",\"name\":\"Report Narrative\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"A stand-alone summary of the entire report's purpose, methodology, findings, conclusions, and recommendations.\",\"howToUse\":\"This should be the last thing that you write. Keep it concise (usually a paragraph or two and always less than a page) to enable the reader to make an informed decision about whether they want to read the report itself.\",\"name\":\"Executive Summary\"},{\"description\":\"Explains the rationale for undertaking the work reported on, the background, and the scope of the report.\",\"howToUse\":\"State what the report is about, define how it meets the requirements of the brief, and explain your research methods.\",\"name\":\"Introduction\"},{\"description\":\"A clear description of how the investigation was carried out and why specific methods were chosen.\",\"howToUse\":\"Write this section concisely but thoroughly. Provide step-by-step details in such a way that a reader could replicate the research you have done.\",\"name\":\"Methods\"},{\"description\":\"A purely factual presentation of the research data using text, graphs, tables, or diagrams.\",\"howToUse\":\"Present the findings of your research as simply as possible. Save your interpretation of the results for the Discussion section.\",\"name\":\"Results and Findings\"},{\"description\":\"The section that brings everything together by showing how the findings relate to the purpose of the report and previous research.\",\"howToUse\":\"Interpret the results, showing how they respond to the brief explained in the introduction. Mention if there were any problems or unexpected results and how they were solved.\",\"name\":\"Discussion\"},{\"description\":\"Suggestions for a future course of action based on the evidence and conclusions.\",\"howToUse\":\"Make recommendations that solve problems or help to develop a new strategy. Make an effort to sound authoritative and certain in your choices.\",\"name\":\"Recommendations\"}]},{\"description\":\"The structural elements required for a reference list entry.\",\"name\":\"Citation Standard\",\"narrativeElements\":[{\"description\":\"The person, group, or organization responsible for the work.\",\"howToUse\":\"Invert authors' names (Lastname, F. M.). Use an ampersand (&) before the final author's name in a list. For groups, use the full name.\",\"name\":\"Author\"},{\"description\":\"The publication date of the work.\",\"howToUse\":\"Enclose the year in parentheses, followed by a period: (2026). For works with no date, use (n.d.).\",\"name\":\"Date\"},{\"description\":\"The name of the specific work being cited.\",\"howToUse\":\"Italicize the title of standalone works (books, reports). Use sentence case—capitalize only the first word of the title and subtitle.\",\"name\":\"Title\"},{\"description\":\"Where the work can be retrieved, such as a journal, publisher, or URL.\",\"howToUse\":\"Include the periodical title and volume/issue if applicable. Provide a DOI or URL as a live link; do not include 'Retrieved from' for most entries.\",\"name\":\"Source\"}]}],\"updatedAt\":\"2023-10-25T00:00:00Z\",\"version\":\"1\"}"}
